Author: Eugeniu Costetchi <costezki.eugen@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 9 21:02:14 2026 +0100

    docs(skills): cap gate runs and narrow checks for small EPICs
    
    Measured over the last 15 sessions: a SMALL EPIC took four clarity-gate
    runs, questions went one dialog at a time, and the full make validate
    ran 223 times while iterating. TINY and SMALL EPICs now run the gate at
    most twice, after which the developer decides the remaining gaps, and an
    accepted gap is recorded as a DEC. Questions are asked in rounds. Narrow
    checks run while iterating and the full gates once per task.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

